1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,680
There is a moment usually quiet, usually late when the performance stops making sense.

2
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:11,520
You have watched someone get torn apart for being real, you have watched the hollow ones

3
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:16,600
get praised and something in you goes still and then cold.

4
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:20,200
This poem came from that moment, not rage, clarity.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,960
So let me read it to you first before I say anything about it.

6
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,000
Let it land on its own.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,720
Making up to a realization about how the world is changing, thoughts driven by exteriority,

8
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:35,320
no care about what lies within.

9
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:40,440
People drooling over aesthetics, shitting all over the hearts of the good ones, praising

10
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:46,960
the false gods, demeaning, deserving humans, talking about love and life, not knowing

11
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,680
the true meaning.

12
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:53,680
How our civilization has turned out, wearing layers of masks themselves, ready to tear

13
00:00:53,680 --> 00:01:00,840
down the true faces, only to make themselves happy, only to make themselves happy.

14
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:07,360
What this does to you, the line that hits hardest, shitting all over the hearts of the

15
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:12,640
good ones, no softening, no metaphor to hide behind.

16
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:18,440
That's what it actually feels like, watching people who show up honestly get dismantled,

17
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:25,280
while the ones performing correctly get lifted, the good ones aren't naive, they are not

18
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:31,520
just willing to trade their interior for uplaws and the world has found a thousand polished

19
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,880
ways to punish that.

20
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:42,120
I felt this most sharply as a creator, the internet says it wants authenticity, right?

21
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:48,400
But the numbers often tell a different story, I spent hours writing essays, poems and videos

22
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:55,400
that came from lived experience, pieces about discipline, relationships, grief, purpose and

23
00:01:55,400 --> 00:02:00,600
the uncomfortable parts of growth, sometimes those barely moved and then I would watch

24
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:07,360
a louder, cleaner, more performative version of the same ideas spread everywhere, not because

25
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:11,800
it was true, because it was easier to consume.

26
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:17,280
There comes a point where every creator has to decide whether they are building a body

27
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:25,600
of work or a costume, the costume usually grows faster, the work lasts longer.

28
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:33,120
And notice, the poem calls this a civilizational thing, how our civilization has turned out,

29
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:39,680
that widening matters, this isn't one person being cruel, it's a system that rewards

30
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:49,400
your surface and calls it culture, there is this mask paradox, here is what cuts deepest,

31
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:55,080
the ones staring down the true faces are themselves masked, they're not confident, they're

32
00:02:55,080 --> 00:03:00,280
defended, there's a difference, confidence doesn't need to flatten anything, defenst

33
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:09,160
as the mask doesn't just hide, it needs to, it needs the authentic face to disappear,

34
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:15,440
because authenticity is an indictment of performance, you can't have both in the same room and

35
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:20,480
pretend they are equal, so the master world doesn't take no genuine people, it goes

36
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:27,480
after them, specifically, deliberately, ready to tear down the true faces, not by accident,

37
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:31,560
I've watched this happen to people who refuse to become characters, some of the most

38
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:37,160
thoughtful people I've met weren't the loudest in the room, they weren't masters of personal

39
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:42,920
branding, they weren't constantly optimizing themselves for approval, they simply cared

40
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:51,120
more about substance than performance, and because of that, they were often overlooked,

41
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:58,160
meanwhile, the people who knew exactly how to package themselves kept receiving the

42
00:03:58,160 --> 00:04:04,400
attention, the opportunities and the praise, not always because they were better, sometimes

43
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:10,320
because they were better at being seen, and that distinction has stayed with me for years,

44
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:16,040
and the ending tells you the motive, only to make themselves happy, only to make themselves

45
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,400
happy, right?

46
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:23,320
Not righteousness, not values, just hunger, wearing borrowed language about love and

47
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:30,360
life, I would like to tell you one thing to carry, this poem does not offer a fix, it offers

48
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:36,920
a name, naming something does not solve it, but it ends a certain confusion, the confusion

49
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:42,240
of thinking you are the problem, when you refuse to wear a mask, you're not, you're just

50
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:48,040
visible in a world that learn to find visibility threatening, so I want to read it one more

51
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:55,760
time, a little bit slower, and listen for that last line doubling, waking up to a realization

52
00:04:55,760 --> 00:05:03,920
about how the world is changing, people drooling over aesthetics, shitting all over the

53
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:09,600
hearts of the court once, wearing layers of masks themselves, ready to tear down the

54
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:16,200
true faces, only to make themselves happy, only to make themselves happy.

55
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:22,240
The waking up in that first line isn't despair, it's the end of being fooled, and that's

56
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:25,520
enough to begin with.

57
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:29,740
This is Breath of Poetry, if this one found a nerve, share it with someone who has been

58
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:36,680
worn down by the performance, not to explain it, just to say it, I see it too, I write things

59
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:41,400
like this every week, things that don't flinch, stay if that's what you have been looking

60
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:41,760
for.

